    "difficulty": "EASY",
    "question": "What is the recommended approach to configure Change Data Feed (CDF) logging for cross-region analytics sharing to reduce storage read latencies?",
    "answer": "### Phase 1: Conceptual Foundation & Core Architecture\nDeploying **Change Data Feed (CDF) logging** within an enterprise environment running **cross-region analytics sharing** requires addressing the critical challenges related to **reduce storage read latencies**. At a high level, **Change Data Feed (CDF) logging** optimizes underlying compute topology, memory buffers, and distributed data structures to isolate workloads and prevent performance degradation. In the context of cross-region analytics sharing, this architectural setup isolates failure domains, prevents resource contention, and guarantees predictable execution latencies.\n\n### Phase 2: Low-Level Mechanics & Implementation\nImplementing this pattern requires the following setup steps and configuration files:\n\n1. **Architecture Setup**: Enable table property `delta.enableChangeDataFeed = true` on target Delta table.\n2. **Implementation Snippet**:\n```sql\n-- Enable Change Data Feed (CDF) to record row-level inserts, updates, and deletes\nALTER TABLE silver.orders\nSET TBLPROPERTIES (delta.enableChangeDataFeed = true);\n\n-- Query incremental changes between commit versions 40 and 45\nSELECT\n    order_id, status, amount,\n    _change_type, _commit_version, _commit_timestamp\nFROM table_changes('silver.orders', 40, 45);\n```\n3. **Parameter Tuning**: Query incremental deltas via `table_changes()` passing commit version or timestamp boundaries.\n\n### Phase 3: Production Hardening & Gotchas\nIn a production environment, several failure states can cause this design to degrade:\n\n- **Storage Overhead from Change Record Retention**: Storing row-level pre/post images increases storage footprint by 20-30%. *Remediation*: Purge change data history during weekly `VACUUM` maintenance cycles.\n- **Missing Delete Tombstones**: Merges without CDF tracking fail to propagate deleted records downstream. *Remediation*: Handle `_change_type = 'delete'` explicitly in downstream consuming pipelines.\n- **CDF Read Timeouts on Huge Version Spans**: Querying 50,000 commit versions simultaneously exhausts driver memory. *Remediation*: Chunk downstream CDF consumer reading windows into bounded batches."
